{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"lMLzKM6IXiYw"},"source":["# RealBasicVSR — Colab Master Setup\n","\n","**Purpose:** Low-resolution video → 4× RealBasicVSR AI upscale → 1688×960 MP4.\n","\n","This notebook is designed to be reused in a new Google Colab account/runtime.\n","\n","**Known working environment**\n","- Python 3.10.x\n","- PyTorch 1.13.1+cu117\n","- torchvision 0.14.1\n","- mmcv-full 1.7.2\n","- mmedit 0.16.1\n","- openmim 0.3.9\n","- NumPy 1.26.4\n","- Tested successfully on Tesla T4\n","\n","**Important:** GPU is required for the AI upscaling step. Final FFmpeg encoding does not require GPU.\n"],"id":"lMLzKM6IXiYw"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"5lSqJgzaXiZE"},"source":["## STEP 0 — Select a GPU runtime\n","\n","In Colab choose **Runtime → Change runtime type → T4 GPU**. Then run the next cell."],"id":"5lSqJgzaXiZE"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"xMJKaGqSXiZL","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790622173093,"user_tz":-360,"elapsed":245,"user":{"displayName":"SHBD USER1","userId":"00577123580696540725"}},"outputId":"b97b0cf8-9150-414f-a44f-3fc89acf14db"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["/bin/bash: line 1: nvidia-smi: command not found\n"]}],"source":["!nvidia-smi"],"id":"xMJKaGqSXiZL"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"f1Xj_F3nXiZR"},"source":["## STEP 1 — Clone RealBasicVSR"],"id":"f1Xj_F3nXiZR"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"eDREaajtXiZU"},"outputs":[],"source":["!git clone https://github.com/ckkelvinchan/RealBasicVSR.git /content/RealBasicVSR\n"],"id":"eDREaajtXiZU"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"6Qez0ddiXiZZ"},"source":["## STEP 2 — Create the known-working Python environment\n","\n","Do not upgrade these packages to newer major versions during this workflow."],"id":"6Qez0ddiXiZZ"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"G0aXOQ9NXiZc"},"outputs":[],"source":["!python3 -m venv /content/rbvsr_legacy\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/python -m pip install --upgrade \"pip<24\"\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/pip install \"numpy==1.26.4\"\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/pip install torch==1.13.1+cu117 torchvision==0.14.1 --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu117\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/pip install openmim==0.3.9\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/mim install \"mmcv-full==1.7.2\"\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/pip install \"mmedit==0.16.1\"\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/pip install opencv-python tqdm\n"],"id":"G0aXOQ9NXiZc"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"JFu_fY8hXiZh"},"source":["## STEP 3 — Verify versions and CUDA\n","\n","Expected: NumPy 1.26.4, Torch 1.13.1+cu117, torchvision 0.14.1, MMCV 1.7.2, MMEdit 0.16.1, and CUDA available = True."],"id":"JFu_fY8hXiZh"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"zzq2O5SAXiZm"},"outputs":[],"source":["!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/python -c \"import sys,torch,torchvision,numpy,mmcv,mmedit; print('Python:',sys.version); print('Torch:',torch.__version__); print('Torchvision:',torchvision.__version__); print('NumPy:',numpy.__version__); print('MMCV:',mmcv.__version__); print('MMEdit:',mmedit.__version__); print('CUDA available:',torch.cuda.is_available()); print('GPU:',torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'NONE')\"\n"],"id":"zzq2O5SAXiZm"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2MXNAUcpXiZr"},"source":["## STEP 4 — Check project files"],"id":"2MXNAUcpXiZr"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Fuc4QbaLXiZu"},"outputs":[],"source":["!ls -lh /content/RealBasicVSR/configs/realbasicvsr_x4.py\n","!ls -lh /content/RealBasicVSR/inference_realbasicvsr.py\n"],"id":"Fuc4QbaLXiZu"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"J0Pq-xazXiZx"},"source":["## STEP 5 — RealBasicVSR checkpoint\n","\n","Place `RealBasicVSR.pth` at:\n","\n","`/content/RealBasicVSR/checkpoints/RealBasicVSR.pth`\n","\n","The checkpoint was previously verified successfully and was about 201 MB.\n"],"id":"J0Pq-xazXiZx"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"lFBMeWmCXiZz"},"outputs":[],"source":["!mkdir -p /content/RealBasicVSR/checkpoints\n","!ls -lh /content/RealBasicVSR/checkpoints/RealBasicVSR.pth\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/python -c \"import torch; p='/content/RealBasicVSR/checkpoints/RealBasicVSR.pth'; x=torch.load(p,map_location='cpu'); print(x.keys())\"\n"],"id":"lFBMeWmCXiZz"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"pmGQt4IZXiZ0"},"source":["## STEP 6 — Upload the input video\n","\n","Use the upload button in the Colab Files panel, or run the next cell.\n","\n","The example below expects:\n","\n","`/content/Hindi Dub_BySHBD 240p.mp4`\n","\n","If your filename is different, change `INPUT` in the later processing cell.\n"],"id":"pmGQt4IZXiZ0"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"JT5-iRJZXiZ2"},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import files\n","uploaded = files.upload()\n","print(\"Uploaded:\", list(uploaded.keys()))\n"],"id":"JT5-iRJZXiZ2"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"LO_MiDPPXiZ4"},"source":["### Check the uploaded video"],"id":"LO_MiDPPXiZ4"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"rrwIJHx7XiZ6"},"outputs":[],"source":["INPUT='/content/Hindi Dub_BySHBD 240p.mp4'\n","!ffprobe -v error -select_streams v:0 -show_entries stream=width,height,r_frame_rate,duration -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 \"$INPUT\"\n"],"id":"rrwIJHx7XiZ6"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"mOQIyc9OXiZ8"},"source":["## STEP 7 — Why this notebook uses one frame at a time\n","\n","We tested multi-frame processing on a Tesla T4. A 5-frame batch caused CUDA out-of-memory, while single-frame inference succeeded.\n","\n","Therefore this notebook uses:\n","\n","**one input frame → one RealBasicVSR inference → immediately save output**\n","\n","This is slower than large batches but is the proven low-memory method for this project.\n","\n","The original approach also accumulated many output tensors in RAM. This notebook avoids that by saving every frame immediately.\n"],"id":"mOQIyc9OXiZ8"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"e7LaFn1pXiZ-"},"source":["## STEP 8 — Create the safe one-frame inference script"],"id":"e7LaFn1pXiZ-"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"NGHDXh0FXiaA"},"outputs":[],"source":["%%writefile /content/RealBasicVSR/inference_frames_safe.py\n","import os, cv2, torch, mmcv\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","from mmcv import Config\n","from mmedit.models import build_model\n","\n","INPUT='/content/Hindi Dub_BySHBD 240p.mp4'\n","OUT='/content/rbvsr_frames'\n","CONFIG='/content/RealBasicVSR/configs/realbasicvsr_x4.py'\n","CHECKPOINT='/content/RealBasicVSR/checkpoints/RealBasicVSR.pth'\n","\n","os.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\n","\n","cfg=Config.fromfile(CONFIG)\n","model=build_model(cfg.model, train_cfg=None, test_cfg=cfg.get('test_cfg'))\n","ck=torch.load(CHECKPOINT, map_location='cpu')\n","model.load_state_dict(ck['state_dict'], strict=False)\n","del ck\n","model=model.cuda().eval()\n","\n","total=int(cv2.VideoCapture(INPUT).get(cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_COUNT))\n","cap=cv2.VideoCapture(INPUT)\n","print('Total frames:', total, flush=True)\n","\n","for n in tqdm(range(total), desc='Upscaling', unit='frame'):\n","    ok, frame=cap.read()\n","    if not ok:\n","        print('Frame read failed:', n, flush=True)\n","        break\n","\n","    img=torch.from_numpy(\n","        cv2.cvtColor(frame, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","    ).float().permute(2,0,1).unsqueeze(0).unsqueeze(0).cuda()/255.0\n","\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        out=model(img, test_mode=True)['output']\n","\n","    result=(\n","        out[0,0].clamp(0,1)\n","        .permute(1,2,0)\n","        .cpu().numpy()*255\n","    ).astype('uint8')\n","\n","    result=cv2.cvtColor(result, cv2.COLOR_RGB2BGR)\n","\n","    cv2.imwrite(\n","        os.path.join(OUT, f'{n:05d}.png'),\n","        result\n","    )\n","\n","    del img,out,result,frame\n","    torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n","\n","cap.release()\n","print('DONE: frames saved to', OUT, flush=True)\n"],"id":"NGHDXh0FXiaA"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"nIVmr2eEXiaD"},"source":["## STEP 9 — Run the AI upscaling\n","\n","Before a fresh run, clear incomplete frames. Then start processing. **Do not interrupt the cell while it is running.**"],"id":"nIVmr2eEXiaD"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"UaRPSXHyXiaF"},"outputs":[],"source":["!rm -rf /content/rbvsr_frames\n","!mkdir -p /content/rbvsr_frames\n","!/content/rbvsr_legacy/bin/python /content/RealBasicVSR/inference_frames_safe.py\n"],"id":"UaRPSXHyXiaF"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"z1PJYJ0lXiaH"},"source":["## STEP 10 — Verify the generated frames\n","\n","For the known test video, the expected count is 485."],"id":"z1PJYJ0lXiaH"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"hOctMK1ZXiaI"},"outputs":[],"source":["!ls /content/rbvsr_frames | wc -l\n"],"id":"hOctMK1ZXiaI"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dRfePmKYXiaK"},"source":["## STEP 11 — Create the upscaled video (GPU NOT required)\n","\n","Only run this after the expected frame count is present.\n","\n","The output resolution for the 422×240 test video is 1688×960.\n"],"id":"dRfePmKYXiaK"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"KyJqHvvDXiaM"},"outputs":[],"source":["!mkdir -p /content/rbvsr_results\n","!ffmpeg -y -framerate 25 -i /content/rbvsr_frames/%05d.png -c:v libx264 -preset veryfast -crf 18 -pix_fmt yuv420p /content/rbvsr_results/upscaled_video.mp4\n"],"id":"KyJqHvvDXiaM"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"tL3LCF3MXiaN"},"source":["## STEP 12 — Add the original audio\n","\n","This copies the source AAC audio without re-encoding it."],"id":"tL3LCF3MXiaN"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Wdtmad2fXiaP"},"outputs":[],"source":["!ffmpeg -y -i /content/rbvsr_results/upscaled_video.mp4 -i \"/content/Hindi Dub_BySHBD 240p.mp4\" -map 0:v:0 -map 1:a:0? -c:v copy -c:a copy -shortest /content/rbvsr_results/Hindi_Dub_BySHBD_4x.mp4\n"],"id":"Wdtmad2fXiaP"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Cvt78v6LXiaR"},"source":["## STEP 13 — Verify the final MP4"],"id":"Cvt78v6LXiaR"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"vI2VADETXiaS"},"outputs":[],"source":["!ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration,size -show_entries stream=index,codec_name,width,height,r_frame_rate -of default=noprint_wrappers=1 /content/rbvsr_results/Hindi_Dub_BySHBD_4x.mp4\n","!ls -lh /content/rbvsr_results/Hindi_Dub_BySHBD_4x.mp4\n"],"id":"vI2VADETXiaS"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"FAgbLzAcXiaU"},"source":["## STEP 14 — Save the final output to Google Drive\n","\n","`/content` is temporary. After a successful run, copy the final MP4 to Google Drive or download it.\n"],"id":"FAgbLzAcXiaU"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"VKsjgh8nXiaV"},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/content/drive')\n"],"id":"VKsjgh8nXiaV"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Yzf6gtviXiaX"},"outputs":[],"source":["!cp /content/rbvsr_results/Hindi_Dub_BySHBD_4x.mp4 /content/drive/MyDrive/\n","!ls -lh /content/drive/MyDrive/Hindi_Dub_BySHBD_4x.mp4\n"],"id":"Yzf6gtviXiaX"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"jHMbrW6eXiaY"},"source":["# Troubleshooting / Known Lessons\n","\n","### NumPy error\n","If you see:\n","`AttributeError: module 'numpy' has no attribute 'bool8'`\n","\n","Use:\n","`numpy==1.26.4`\n","\n","### Wrong max sequence argument\n","The repository's argument is:\n","`--max_seq_len`\n","\n","not:\n","`--max-seq-len`\n","\n","However, this master workflow does not depend on that argument because it uses the safe one-frame script.\n","\n","### GPU unavailable\n","If:\n","`nvidia-smi: command not found`\n","\n","the current runtime has no GPU. Do not start AI processing.\n","\n","If Colab reports:\n","`Cannot connect to GPU backend`\n","\n","GPU access is temporarily unavailable/limited. Try another eligible runtime/account or wait.\n","\n","### Colab runtime reset\n","Files under `/content` can disappear after a reset. The 485 frames are temporary unless copied to persistent storage.\n","\n","### Heredoc error\n","Avoid:\n","`!python - <<'PY'`\n","\n","Use the `%%writefile` cell provided in this notebook.\n","\n","### 5-frame CUDA OOM\n","Do not change the safe processor to large frame batches on a T4. Single-frame inference was the proven successful method.\n","\n","# Known Successful Test\n","\n","Input:\n","- 422×240\n","- 25 FPS\n","- 19.4 seconds\n","- 485 frames\n","\n","GPU:\n","- Tesla T4\n","\n","Successful environment:\n","- Python 3.10.12\n","- PyTorch 1.13.1+cu117\n","- torchvision 0.14.1\n","- mmcv-full 1.7.2\n","- mmedit 0.16.1\n","- openmim 0.3.9\n","- NumPy 1.26.4\n","\n","Successful AI run:\n","- 485 frames\n","- 4× upscale\n","- 1688×960\n","- about 3m54s\n","- about 2.07 frames/sec\n","\n","**END OF MASTER NOTEBOOK**\n"],"id":"jHMbrW6eXiaY"}],"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"gpuType":"T4","runtime_attributes":{"runtime_version":"2026.07"}},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"},"accelerator":"GPU"},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}